CORE
main.cpp

^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ four levels: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The runaway-recursion guard in elaborate_class_template counted every
enclosing instance of the same template; it now counts only those whose
arguments the new ones grow from (template_args_may_recurse: an argument
contains the enclosing one, or one argument list is a prefix or suffix of
the other).  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only
its WRONG assertion.
